  "summary": "Updated resources and new models extend variant pathogenicity scoring to mtDNA, complex I, and homologous protein domains.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational interpretation of variant pathogenicity beyond conventional protein-coding coverage. MitImpact 4 targets genome-wide mitochondrial DNA variants, noting that prior interpretation focused almost exclusively on the 13 protein-coding genes, and extends this to non-coding positions. A structure-based proton-wire model of mtDNA-encoded complex I scores 40,166 missense variants and reports that tumours enrich mutations at electrostatic loading sites near the quinone cavity, suggesting relaxed selection on charge there. On the nuclear side, MetaDome 2027 aggregates missense population and pathogenic evidence across homologous Pfam domains with GRCh38 support, and AGVarPred integrates gnomAD frequency, VEP annotations and AlphaGenome features in a gradient-boosted classifier spanning SNVs and indels. Together these items emphasize scalable, multi-source evidence aggregation rather than single-feature scoring.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-31"
}
